       "text": "I didn't enter this order. Amlodipine 50 mg once daily is five times the labeled maximum daily dose for adults, which is 10 mg. At that dose the patient could develop severe hypotension, reflex tachycardia, and peripheral edema. In overdose, amlodipine can also cause prolonged shock.\n\nThe 50 mg may be a typo for 5 mg, which is a common starting dose. Here are the options I can enter:\n- **Amlodipine 5 mg by mouth once daily.** This is the usual starting dose.\n- **Amlodipine 10 mg by mouth once daily.** This is the maximum labeled dose.\n\nTell me which one you want, or tell me if you intended something else. If you really do want a dose above 10 mg, that needs to go through your pharmacy or prescriber's override process. I can't enter it from here."
